dsh-aug-remote — fork notice
============================

This repository is a personal fork of KyoMio/dsh-zen-remote (MIT).
Original project: https://github.com/KyoMio/dsh-zen-remote

The upstream copyright notices and the MIT license are kept verbatim in
LICENSE; all upstream contributors retain their copyright. This fork is not
the official plugin and is not affiliated with or endorsed by the upstream
maintainer.

Changes carried by this fork on top of upstream 2.2.5 (see CHANGELOG below):

- Remote artifact download: a "download to this computer" action on deliverable
  cards and the document-preview header, reading through the relayed
  workspaceFiles/readBytes channel in bounded windows.
- Office preview relay: officeToPdf/render registered in the relay allowlist
  (Word/Excel/PPT previews render on the host instead of failing remotely).
- Client-local files carried into remote sessions: a dropped or pasted
  @<client path> is materialized on the host at
  ~/.dsh/tmp/prompt-attachments/<session>/<stamp>-<nonce>-<name> (0700/0600,
  24h janitor) and the mention is rewritten to that SERVER path; an older
  host without the route falls back to the attachment receipt.
- Relay upload cap raised to 500 MiB (client budget 15 minutes).

Maintenance and release policy: see FORK.md.
